{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1003596-what-level-spheres-would-i-need-to-do-the-following","id":1003596,"title":"What level spheres would I need to do the following?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-15T14:13:31-08:00","id":1003596,"title":"What level spheres would I need to do the following?","content":"<br /> At what rank in life and or spirit would someone have to get to be able to make ents (essentially, bestowing spirits into trees or other objects such as rocks and making them get up and do your bidding?)<br /> <br /> Also, at what rank in spirit would I need to imprison a being (werewolf) inside the Gauntlet?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T15:15:16-08:00","id":1003632,"title":"","content":"Spirit 4 for both is the simplest way.<br /> <br /> For the ent you create a tree fetish.<br /> For the fera you weave the gauntlet around him.<br /> Better would be Correspondence 4 to cut them from the normal plane of existence. Better still would be Correspondence+Spirit 4.<br /> <br /> You could do an ent without conscience if you just go for animation, Life 3 could be enough (depends on playstyle).<br /> A relative safe bet would be Life3 + Time 3. This way you let the tree grow in position really fast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T21:31:51-08:00","id":1003775,"title":"","content":"You could also make Ents with Prime 5 and Mind 5, but obviously not many mages will have both. Spirit is an under-appreciated Sphere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T01:16:05-08:00","id":1003816,"title":"","content":"Technically Life 2 + Time 3 should be enough to make the tree grow quickly. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T05:10:45-08:00","id":1003870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1003596-what-level-spheres-would-i-need-to-do-the-following?p=1003632#post1003632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could do an ent without conscience if you just go for animation, Life 3 could be enough (depends on playstyle).</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. Could you say more about this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T06:58:14-08:00","id":1003914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1003596-what-level-spheres-would-i-need-to-do-the-following?p=1003870#post1003870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm. Could you say more about this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Assuming HAB/RBD you could justify doing damage by assaulting them with a tree.<br /> <br /> Under HAB/PBD it is not so easy but still...<br /> Creating a plant from scratch(or any other simple life forms) would be Life 3 and Prime 2.<br /> Since the tree is already there you can drop the prime and transform the tree into a moving tree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T07:14:35-08:00","id":1003923,"title":"","content":"Since you're asking for a tree that can independently act and attack things, Spirit 4 or Mind 5 is the rule here. Either you use a pre-existing mind in the form of the spirit (and hope you find the right spirit and that it likes you enough to do what you want), or you just make a new mind to your needs and install it.<br /> <br /> The other stuff in the thread would let you attack people using the tree, but I don't think that's what you want. Life lets the tree grow quickly or move in a way trees normally can't, but trees aren't conscious enough to do anything with those new abilities without you actively controlling them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7356-haldir2012","name":"haldir2012","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T07:35:23-08:00","id":1003931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haldir2012</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1003596-what-level-spheres-would-i-need-to-do-the-following?p=1003923#post1003923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since you're asking for a tree that can independently act and attack things, Spirit 4 or Mind 5 is the rule here. Either you use a pre-existing mind in the form of the spirit (and hope you find the right spirit and that it likes you enough to do what you want), or you just make a new mind to your needs and install it.<br /> <br /> The other stuff in the thread would let you attack people using the tree, but I don't think that's what you want. Life lets the tree grow quickly or move in a way trees normally can't, but trees aren't conscious enough to do anything with those new abilities without you actively controlling them.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you can (or have to) live with actively controlling it, then Multitasking with Mind 1 combined with Life/Time is the way with the least requirements that fulfill practically every objective the more advanced rotes do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T07:55:06-08:00","id":1003937,"title":"","content":"Couldn't Life give some very basic instincts to objects?<br /> Like, survival instinct of attacking as a way of defence. You don't need a conscience to do this even our cells work this way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T08:50:37-08:00","id":1003959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1003596-what-level-spheres-would-i-need-to-do-the-following?p=1003937#post1003937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Couldn't Life give some very basic instincts to objects?<br /> Like, survival instinct of attacking as a way of defence. You don't need a conscience to do this even our cells work this way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course, but if these instincts act in a way beneficial to you...<br /> Is up to the ST.<br /> I would be more comfortable with actively piloting the tree with Multitasking.<br /> <br /> Another possible way would be that of familiardom. In FbDF are several ways presented to grant your familiar a body.<br /> <br /> And I want to point out, that Spirit 4 is only required if the spirit is unwilling or can not take possession itself, or can't cross the gauntlet because it is too thick. If the Spirit can do it with its own power then Spirit 2 (to call it) is enough.<br /> <br /> Regarding Mind, 5 is only required for human level and up, animal level should be 4.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T11:20:03-08:00","id":1004020,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12022_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12022\" data-vbnamecard=\"12022\">Nonsense</a>, I don't think the fact that the character is going to benefited shoukd change the spheres required. <br /> I agree that there are better ways, but when you don't have Mind nor Spirit, toss the plant/statue/chair into someone and make it fight for its new Life..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T12:45:24-08:00","id":1004064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haldir2012</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1003596-what-level-spheres-would-i-need-to-do-the-following?p=1003923#post1003923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since you're asking for a tree that can independently act and attack things, Spirit 4 or Mind 5 is the rule here. Either you use a pre-existing mind in the form of the spirit (and hope you find the right spirit and that it likes you enough to do what you want), or you just make a new mind to your needs and install it.<br /> <br /> The other stuff in the thread would let you attack people using the tree, but I don't think that's what you want. Life lets the tree grow quickly or move in a way trees normally can't, but trees aren't conscious enough to do anything with those new abilities without you actively controlling them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Alternatively, you could use Spirit to rouse the spirit of the tree, but yeah, you'd still be in the situation where you don't know what kind of consciousness you're going to get out of it. It's just as likely that a tree spirit is unlikely to act with any haste, or even see a necessity for movement at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6384-frozenfishy","name":"Frozenfishy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T10:47:03-08:00","id":1004525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1003596-what-level-spheres-would-i-need-to-do-the-following?p=1004020#post1004020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span>, I don't think the fact that the character is going to benefited shoukd change the spheres required. <br /> I agree that there are better ways, but when you don't have Mind nor Spirit, toss the plant/statue/chair into someone and make it fight for its new Life..</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you elaborate on that, please?<br /> I didn't get it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T20:14:38-08:00","id":1004777,"title":"","content":"So, if I wanted to command an army of ents I could use spirit 4 and Life 3 (or four) to bind the spirits into the trees and make the trees rise out of the ground and fight?<br /> <br /> Also, what level Spirit (or any other sphere) would I need to command a spirit/use a spirit to attack/kill someone/defend me? For example, my character is a folk singer Dreamspeaker who often fights using his banjo. So what level spirit sphere would I need to use the banjo to send a string-like spirit towards someone to strangle them, or perhaps have said spirit erect a defense for me?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T22:50:59-08:00","id":1004814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingJohn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1003596-what-level-spheres-would-i-need-to-do-the-following?p=1004777#post1004777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, if I wanted to command an army of ents I could use spirit 4 and Life 3 (or four) to bind the spirits into the trees and make the trees rise out of the ground and fight?</div> </div> </div> </div>Spirit alone could be enough, but an army is definitely requiring lots of successes... i.e. godlike feat<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingJohn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1003596-what-level-spheres-would-i-need-to-do-the-following?p=1004777#post1004777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, what level Spirit (or any other sphere) would I need to command a spirit/use a spirit to attack/kill someone/defend me? For example, my character is a folk singer Dreamspeaker who often fights using his banjo. So what level spirit sphere would I need to use the banjo to send a string-like spirit towards someone to strangle them, or perhaps have said spirit erect a defense for me?</div> </div> </div> </div>At 3 almost all spheres can do Damage. So I would use 3. Difficulty is the gauntlet rating with a minimum of 3+X (x depending on vulgarity).<br /> For the defense you should have worked out the Spirit you intend to use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T23:48:55-08:00","id":1004819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1003596-what-level-spheres-would-i-need-to-do-the-following?p=1004814#post1004814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spirit alone could be enough, but an army is definitely requiring lots of successes... i.e. godlike feat</div> </div> </div> </div>This assumes the spirit(s) in question possess(ess) the ability to animate their wooden vessel. Trees, after all, can't normally move, even if there's an intelligence at the head. If the spirit doesn't have that power, you'd need Life 3 to afford it the animating ability it requires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T02:37:12-08:00","id":1004848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1003596-what-level-spheres-would-i-need-to-do-the-following?p=1004819#post1004819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This assumes the spirit(s) in question possess(ess) the ability to animate their wooden vessel. Trees, after all, can't normally move, even if there's an intelligence at the head. If the spirit doesn't have that power, you'd need Life 3 to afford it the animating ability it requires.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hence the \u201ccould\u201c\ud83d\ude0a","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T07:14:58-08:00","id":1004921,"title":"","content":"I remember some rote at Spirit 3 or 4 that basically bound a bunch of spirits unwillingly into your opponent's body like a fetish, and they would deal aggravated damage as they tried to get out. Can't find it now though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7356-haldir2012","name":"haldir2012","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T20:26:58-08:00","id":1005212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1003596-what-level-spheres-would-i-need-to-do-the-following?p=1004814#post1004814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spirit alone could be enough, but an army is definitely requiring lots of successes... i.e. godlike feat<br /> <br /> <br /> At 3 almost all spheres can do Damage. So I would use 3. Difficulty is the gauntlet rating with a minimum of 3+X (x depending on vulgarity).<br /> For the defense you should have worked out the Spirit you intend to use.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, I would need spirit 3 to bind a string spirit to a banjo and use it to attack?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T20:55:23-08:00","id":1005220,"title":"","content":"I think that would require Spirit 4.<br /> <br /> Thinking outside the box, if you used Spirit 2 to awaken the spirit of a tree, couldn't you use Correspondence 3 or Forces 2 to grant it the ability to move, at least temporarily?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T23:43:24-08:00","id":1005259,"title":"","content":"Rousing Spirits needs Rank 3.<br /> Binding Spirits needs Rank 4.<br /> If you do chiminage Rank 2 can be enough.<br /> If the spirit in question has the ability to possess the tree/banjo and animate it within his own power.<br /> <br /> Rousing the spirit of a tree might also do the trick. In the sphere description is an example of a house getting animated (vulgar of course).<br /> <br /> Instead of binding a spirit to thre banjo why not rouse it. Over time and provided with occasional re-rousals the spirit can get mighty enough.<br /> Take the banjo as unique instrument, develop a little backstory and you should be golden. Be prepared for a lot of dox, tough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T12:27:09-08:00","id":1005800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1003596-what-level-spheres-would-i-need-to-do-the-following?p=1005259#post1005259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rousing Spirits needs Rank 3.<br /> Binding Spirits needs Rank 4.<br /> If you do chiminage Rank 2 can be enough.<br /> If the spirit in question has the ability to possess the tree/banjo and animate it within his own power.<br /> <br /> Rousing the spirit of a tree might also do the trick. In the sphere description is an example of a house getting animated (vulgar of course).<br /> <br /> Instead of binding a spirit to thre banjo why not rouse it. Over time and provided with occasional re-rousals the spirit can get mighty enough.<br /> Take the banjo as unique instrument, develop a little backstory and you should be golden. Be prepared for a lot of dox, tough.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://reference.l2fury.com/index.php/Spirit_3\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://reference.l2fury.com/index.php/Spirit_3\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://reference.l2fury.com/index.php/Spirit_3\" target=\"_blank\"> http://reference.l2fury.com/index.php/Spirit_3 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> What does this ^ mean when it says this:<br /> <br /> &quot;While in the spirit worlds, the mage obeys the laws of those places and interacts with them normally. The mage can deal directly with spirits, <b>but he can also exert his magic directly against them. </b>&quot;<br /> <br /> How would a spirit mage exert his power against a spirit? Could he tear it apart and make it dissipate into nothingness? I know that he could put it to sleep, but yeah.<br /> <br /> And two<br /> <br /> &quot;As the mage can alter the spirit world directly, he can also stir a spirit to wakefulness or lure it into slumber. Most objects and places have associated spirits, but the powerful Gauntlet and lack of connection to the mortal world causes those spirits to sleep, uninterested ingoings-on around them. The mage can stir those that hover on the edge of wakefulness, or briefly cause some to return to sleep. Most spirits are too weak, too far deteriorated and too unconscious to be so roused, but many places or items that hover on the edge of importance or that have strong Resonance have lightly sleeping spirits that can be roused. Similarly, powerful objects or fetishes have spirits that the mage can put to sleep temporarily, perhaps to avoid their wrath or to reach something that they guard&quot;<br /> <br /> This dosn't necessarily mean that he can control them. If I stir up a spirit with my banjo, how am I sure I can control it and use it to do my bidding without spirit 4?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T13:00:42-08:00","id":1005822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingJohn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1003596-what-level-spheres-would-i-need-to-do-the-following?p=1005800#post1005800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://reference.l2fury.com/index.php/Spirit_3\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://reference.l2fury.com/index.php/Spirit_3\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://reference.l2fury.com/index.php/Spirit_3\" target=\"_blank\"> http://reference.l2fury.com/index.php/Spirit_3 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> What does this ^ mean when it says this:<br /> <br /> &quot;While in the spirit worlds, the mage obeys the laws of those places and interacts with them normally. The mage can deal directly with spirits, <b>but he can also exert his magic directly against them. </b>&quot;<br /> <br /> How would a spirit mage exert his power against a spirit? Could he tear it apart and make it dissipate into nothingness? I know that he could put it to sleep, but yeah.<br /> <br /> And two<br /> <br /> &quot;As the mage can alter the spirit world directly, he can also stir a spirit to wakefulness or lure it into slumber. Most objects and places have associated spirits, but the powerful Gauntlet and lack of connection to the mortal world causes those spirits to sleep, uninterested ingoings-on around them. The mage can stir those that hover on the edge of wakefulness, or briefly cause some to return to sleep. Most spirits are too weak, too far deteriorated and too unconscious to be so roused, but many places or items that hover on the edge of importance or that have strong Resonance have lightly sleeping spirits that can be roused. Similarly, powerful objects or fetishes have spirits that the mage can put to sleep temporarily, perhaps to avoid their wrath or to reach something that they guard&quot;<br /> <br /> This dosn't necessarily mean that he can control them. If I stir up a spirit with my banjo, how am I sure I can control it and use it to do my bidding without spirit 4?</div> </div> </div> </div>1. When in the Middle Umbra, Spirit magic can work life Life magic or Matter magic does in the mundane world. So Spirit 2 can be used to melt and reform and influence spiritual plants, Spirit 3 can be used to heal or harm spirits directly, as well as turn ephemeral rock into ephemeral mist.<br /> <br /> 2. You're right, without Spirit 4 you can't control your new Banjo Buddy, you'll just have to be nice to them and hope it responds in kind. That being said, when relatively new objects are spiritually awakened, they don't really have a strong personality as such, and will have to gain one over time. If you banjo is an antique, however, it probably has a very well defined personality and can remember back to all the years of music its played, and may have gained a certain preference for a particular style of music. Make no mistake, it's still a banjo, it's just a little sentient now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T13:38:38-08:00","id":1005839,"title":"","content":"From what I've read, objects that have been awakened by Mages tend to like that Mage. Then again, that's also because the usual act of awakening a spirit involves treating it well, keeping it repaired, and talking to it. So naturally an object will be more fond of the Mage. This is the primary advantage of waking up one's possessions: they are aware and well-disposed towards their owner, so they work towards the Mage's advantage.<br /> <br /> Of course, unless the object and spirit are old (like the antique banjo above), well loved, or particularly significant (for example, a prop from a well received film, or the weapon in a high profile murder), the spirits found in objects will tend to be fairly weak. They won't have too strong a personality, and could only do so much for their owner. Still, a gun that never jams, or a computer that tells the user when it's being hacked, is a valuable item on its own.<br /> <br /> Plus, awakened objects have a presence in the Umbra. They naturally affect spirits (so you can attack a ghost with an awakened knife), and can be brought along for a stepping sideways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T00:38:30-08:00","id":1007082,"title":"","content":"So<br /> <br /> What would I need to roll to create and command a tree fetish (or any fetish) to attack someone?<br /> <br /> And would it be possible to summon a spirit of ice, or a spirit of fire and command it to do my bidding with just spirit 4, or would I need forces?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T00:54:29-08:00","id":1007088,"title":"","content":"Also, about LIFE 3:<br /> <br /> &quot;Advanced understanding allows the mage to radically alter simple organisms (turning a tree inside-out); transform one into another (changing fruit into insects); or \u2013 with Prime 2 \u2013 conjure them from raw energy.<br /> <br /> Working with his own Pattern, that mage can work substantial alterations on himself, growing gills, claws, armor and so forth. He remains essentially human, but begins to master the definition of \u201chuman.\u201d <b>Meanwhile, he also gains the ability to heal damage to other complex organisms, put them to sleep, or inflict harm upon their living Pattern forms.</b>&quot;<br /> <br /> So would this mean using Life 3 you could inflict damage upon other living things (such as humans, werewolves, etc)?<br /> <br /> And by patterns, that could mean using your magic to interrupt their blood flow/clog their pipes, making them stop breathing, making their legs inoperable, so on?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T03:24:47-08:00","id":1007129,"title":"","content":"Yes to your two Life 3 questions.<br /> <br /> Fetish Creation<br /> 1. Find a suitable spirit<br /> 2. Bring him to comply with your intention<br /> 3. Help him out if necessary<br /> 4. Attune to the Fetish<br /> 5. Activate the Fetish<br /> 6. Command it to attack<br /> <br /> Which stats to roll?<br /> Depends heavily on the chosen method:<br /> If you want a special spirit it stands to reason that a few rolls on int+cosmology/esoterica are in order.<br /> Then you can summon him, or better seek him out.<br /> You can intomidate him, beat him to submission, coerce him with a service of mutual benefit.<br /> If he can't posess the tree himself you have to help him out with Spirit 4.<br /> To Attune a fetish you have to roll Willpower with a difficulty equal to the Gnosis of the spirit.<br /> If you have tricked the spirit into tje fetish(or are on his bad side for other reasons) then it might require a turn until the command gets executed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-24T01:34:43-08:00","id":1007614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1003596-what-level-spheres-would-i-need-to-do-the-following?p=1007129#post1007129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes to your two Life 3 questions.<br /> <br /> Fetish Creation<br /> 1. Find a suitable spirit<br /> 2. Bring him to comply with your intention<br /> 3. Help him out if necessary<br /> 4. Attune to the Fetish<br /> 5. Activate the Fetish<br /> 6. Command it to attack<br /> <br /> Which stats to roll?<br /> Depends heavily on the chosen method:<br /> If you want a special spirit it stands to reason that a few rolls on int+cosmology/esoterica are in order.<br /> Then you can summon him, or better seek him out.<br /> You can intomidate him, beat him to submission, coerce him with a service of mutual benefit.<br /> If he can't posess the tree himself you have to help him out with Spirit 4.<br /> To Attune a fetish you have to roll Willpower with a difficulty equal to the Gnosis of the spirit.<br /> If you have tricked the spirit into tje fetish(or are on his bad side for other reasons) then it might require a turn until the command gets executed.</div> </div> </div> </div>In a fight, what would I roll if I were using, say, a warrior woman garish that wielded a spear?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-24T03:32:06-08:00","id":1007636,"title":"","content":"I can not recommend to try to make a Fetish while in a Fight.<br /> <br /> English is not my first language, I have no clue what garish means in this context (google-fu failed me).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T22:40:00-08:00","id":1008424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1003596-what-level-spheres-would-i-need-to-do-the-following?p=1007636#post1007636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can not recommend to try to make a Fetish while in a Fight.<br /> <br /> English is not my first language, I have no clue what garish means in this context (google-fu failed me).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Gah-..this is why spirit is a hard sphere to understand......<br /> <br /> I mean, what if I create a fetish before the fight? What would I need to roll to invoke it into the fight and make it fight for me?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T03:13:44-08:00","id":1008469,"title":"","content":"That is an entire chapter from Forged by Dragons Fire.<br /> It depends on your Focus.<br /> Can you give me more details on your mage?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T04:57:31-08:00","id":1008494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1003596-what-level-spheres-would-i-need-to-do-the-following?p=1008469#post1008469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is an entire chapter from Forged by Dragons Fire.<br /> It depends on your Focus.<br /> Can you give me more details on your mage?</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you suggest what I could read to gain an indepth knowledge of all things spirit, so I can rp the dreamspeaker efficiently?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T14:16:54-08:00","id":1008679,"title":"","content":"Pages 31 to 39 of FbDF (Fetish Creation)<br /> The Infinite Tapestry<br /> The Book of World<br /> Tradbook Dreamspeaker<br /> <br /> It is not mandatory to know all the books to rp a Dreamspeaker.<br /> Chiminage and a little on Practice ought to be enough.<br /> <br /> Edit: Spirit Ways is also a good read.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":12022,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","user":"Nonsense","date":". 11-28-2016, 02:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T14:10:56-08:00","id":1009046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1003596-what-level-spheres-would-i-need-to-do-the-following?p=1004814#post1004814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spirit alone could be enough, but an army is definitely requiring lots of successes... i.e. godlike feat<br /> <br /> <br /> At 3 almost all spheres can do Damage. So I would use 3. Difficulty is the gauntlet rating with a minimum of 3+X (x depending on vulgarity).<br /> For the defense you should have worked out the Spirit you intend to use.</div> </div> </div> </div>How do you do that mentions a few scenarios in which Spirit may need to be combined with other spheres.<br /> <br /> If I allied with a flesh-eating spirit or a wolf spirit, would I need to use spirit 3 and prime something to get them to help me out, since the flesh-eating spirit would have a physical effect (I'd assume I would need prime)<br /> <br /> Essentially, if I try to get a spirit to attack something or someone, can I just use the spirit sphere and nothing else?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T23:57:32-08:00","id":1009211,"title":"","content":"You can, if the ST allows it.<br /> \ud83d\ude09","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T21:48:37-08:00","id":1010506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1003596-what-level-spheres-would-i-need-to-do-the-following?p=1009211#post1009211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can, if the ST allows it.<br /> \ud83d\ude09</div> </div> </div> </div>So, if I wanted to create man-eating plants, giant spiders, and ents I would need life 3, right? And without them possessing their own conscious, they'd essentially be under my control, yes?<br /> <br /> In regards to spirits, I could summon a spirit tree and make a pact with it to fight for me, or an equivilient of a plant warrior from the umbra, yes? And if so, what would be the difference in what a spirit man-eating plant could do as opposed to one that I manufacture using life?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T22:28:45-08:00","id":1010522,"title":"","content":"The main difference is control. Life created plantattacks without consciousness need your action to act, albeit you could use Mind 1 to Multitask.<br /> The spirit plant is acting without needing constant commands.<br /> <br /> Mechanically the damage calculation can be different.<br /> Life could be successes x 2 (Arete roll)<br /> Spirit rolls his own Rage with 1 Damage per success.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T23:32:29-08:00","id":1010532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1003596-what-level-spheres-would-i-need-to-do-the-following?p=1010522#post1010522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The main difference is control. Life created plantattacks without consciousness need your action to act, albeit you could use Mind 1 to Multitask.<br /> The spirit plant is acting without needing constant commands.<br /> <br /> Mechanically the damage calculation can be different.<br /> Life could be successes x 2 (Arete roll)<br /> Spirit rolls his own Rage with 1 Damage per success.</div> </div> </div> </div>To make a pact with a spirit I obviously need spirit 2, however, would I be able to use spirit 3 or spirit 2, or spirit sphere alone to have said spirit fight for me/defend me outside of the umbra?<br /> <br /> Also, would the spirits be able to materalize visibly, or would they be fighting for me invisibly?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T23:59:15-08:00","id":1010540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingJohn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1003596-what-level-spheres-would-i-need-to-do-the-following?p=1010532#post1010532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To make a pact with a spirit I obviously need spirit 2, however, would I be able to use spirit 3 or spirit 2, or spirit sphere alone to have said spirit fight for me/defend me outside of the umbra?<br /> <br /> Also, would the spirits be able to materalize visibly, or would they be fighting for me invisibly?</div> </div> </div> </div>Spirit 2 allows you to converse with a spirit. Whether the spirit will then fight for you depends on how persuasive you can be.<br /> <br /> To what degree a spirit can defend you outside the Umbra depends on the spirit's individual Charm loadout. It needs Materialize in order to do what it says on the tin, and it needs Charms devoted to effecting change in the material world to do that. A plant spirit might have a Charm for getting all plants in the vicinity to lash out against a target of the spirit's choice, for instance.<br /> <br /> If the spirit has neither of those things, then it can't help the Mage. It's as straight forward as that. Either it can, or it can't. The use of Life and Spirit to put the umbrood into a physical body for a time can overcome these limitations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T06:21:41-08:00","id":1010600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1003596-what-level-spheres-would-i-need-to-do-the-following?p=1010540#post1010540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spirit 2 allows you to converse with a spirit. Whether the spirit will then fight for you depends on how persuasive you can be.<br /> <br /> To what degree a spirit can defend you outside the Umbra depends on the spirit's individual Charm loadout. It needs Materialize in order to do what it says on the tin, and it needs Charms devoted to effecting change in the material world to do that. A plant spirit might have a Charm for getting all plants in the vicinity to lash out against a target of the spirit's choice, for instance.<br /> <br /> If the spirit has neither of those things, then it can't help the Mage. It's as straight forward as that. Either it can, or it can't. The use of Life and Spirit to put the umbrood into a physical body for a time can overcome these limitations.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, what if I ally with a wolf spirit, it wouldn't be able to attack/defend by its lonesome? It needs some form of surrounding?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T12:56:40-08:00","id":1010777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingJohn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1003596-what-level-spheres-would-i-need-to-do-the-following?p=1010600#post1010600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, what if I ally with a wolf spirit, it wouldn't be able to attack/defend by its lonesome? It needs some form of surrounding?</div> </div> </div> </div>What? &quot;Form of surrounding&quot;? I don't know what that's supposed to mean.<br /> <br /> What I mean is, spirits have powers called Charms. One of them - Materialize - lets the spirit manifest physically in the material world. Other Charms directly effect the material world in some way. If the wolf spirit has neither Materialize nor any sort of Charm capable of affecting your side of the Gauntlet, then it cannot attack or defend you when outside the Umbra. Not unless you have the magick necessary to provide a physical presence in your world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}